{
  "format": "mistudio.decision-precedence-cases/1",
  "owner": "miStudio (feature 040 S2, services/probe_monitor_metrics.deployed_decision); vendored by miLLM",
  "rule": [
    "Inputs: the probe's global bar (probe.threshold), its length bands (probe.length_bands), its scope (probe.scope, a contract scope), the window being judged (null = the probe's own scope), that window's entry from decision.windows (window_entry: {threshold, length_bands}, or null), and the number of scored tokens (n_scored).",
    "own = window_entry.threshold (null when there is no entry). bar = own when not null, else probe.threshold. base rule = window_bar when own is not null, else global when bar is not null, else none.",
    "A band table (probe.length_bands, or window_entry.length_bands) is used whole or not at all: it is treated as empty unless every band has a numeric threshold (not null), an integer min_tokens >= 0 and a max_tokens that is null or an integer, and the last band is open-ended (max_tokens null). This is the table a server arms; a table it would not arm decides nothing.",
    "A band table matches n_scored with the first band where min_tokens <= n_scored and (max_tokens is null or n_scored <= max_tokens). A matched band sets the bar to its threshold.",
    "1. When own is not null and window_entry.length_bands is non-empty: a matching band gives rule window_band; no matching band gives the base rule and the bar.",
    "2. Otherwise, when the window is the probe's own scope (window null or equal to probe.scope) and (own is null or probe.scope is \"all\") and probe.length_bands is non-empty: a matching band gives rule probe_band.",
    "3. Otherwise: the base rule and the bar.",
    "expect.threshold null means no bar: the probe does not fire. A probe fires when score >= threshold."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
